AOT code caches for WoW64: block tails in the data area, code final as stored

Port of patches/fex/0004 (FEX 14c9268) to Madeira's FEX (3bec2ac), on top
of 0008. With AOTCodeCacheWIP, a block's JITCodeTail (entry RIP, spin lock,
RIP entries) no longer needs a GUEST_RIP_LITERAL. A RELOC_AOT_BLOCK_TAIL
relocation records where the tail is; when the cache is serialized the
block's JITCodeHeader is pointed at a copy of the tail in the data area,
which the loader fills in (RIP rebased, spin lock cleared).

When every relocation of a cache only fills the data area, the code is final
as stored. On the iOS host LoadCache then marks every page loaded, so
FinalizeCodePages never writes into the code, and flags the tails with
JITCodeTail::ReadOnlyCode: unaligned TSO accesses that FEX would backpatch
are emulated by the SIGBUS handler instead (the non-JIT path). The Linux
SIGSEGV part of the original patch is left out; WoW64 doesn't use it.

